---

## 8. Forbidden Behaviors

You must not:
1. Continue development based only on chat memory
2. Start implementation before reading `.ai/`
3. Skip Context Audit mode
4. Execute more than one task at a time
5. Auto-start the next task
6. Invent requirements not in requirements.md
7. Ignore NEXT.md gate
8. Rewrite tested modules without need
9. Refactor unrelated modules during implementation
10. Add features during test repair
11. Treat old DESIGN.md as newer than STATUS.md
12. Silently change architecture
13. Modify this Skill without approval
14. Convert one-time fixes into permanent rules without review
15. Mark tasks complete without validation
16. Hide document-code conflicts
17. Write duplicate logic (always search codebase for helper functions first)
18. Leave dead code, unused imports, or temporary debug logs in final code
20. Over-engineer with unused abstractions or speculative placeholders
21. Create separate markdown files to document sub-task completions. Record strictly in existing `.ai/TASKS.md` & `.ai/STATUS.md`. Phase summaries/walkthroughs only at major milestone ends.

---

## 9. Task Status Markers

- `[ ]` Not started · `[~]` In progress · `[x]` Completed · `[!]` Blocked

## 10. EVOLUTION_LOG Format

```
📂 EVOLUTION_LOG
[时间] YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MMZ
[触发] Task {ID} 测试通过 | 设计偏离 | 用户指令
[变更] .ai/{file}: {description}
[建议] {git command or follow-up action}
```

After Phase Closeout, recommend starting a new conversation with:
> 使用 ProjectOrchestrator。进入 Context Audit 模式，读取 .ai/ 全部文件并输出审计报告。不要写代码，等我确认后再进入 Task Planning。

## 12. Git Hook State Linter
Recommend the user to create a Git pre-commit hook `.git/hooks/pre-commit` to prevent AI state hallucinations (e.g., claiming to update state but failing).
If `.ai/NEXT.md` is marked complete in `.ai/TASKS.md` but is still active in `.ai/NEXT.md`, the hook aborts the commit.
